<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24512" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">interversĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		interverto. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>An overthrowing</i>, <i>frustrating</i>, <i>thwarting</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedicationis (Christi),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 1, 20</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A purloining</i>, <i>pilfering</i>,
				<i>embezzling</i>: de interversione convictus,
			Cod. 10, 70, 12.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
